WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.647
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 1. Topic: Making the Subject of a Formula. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:17.083
Make m the subject of the formula m over 2 minus 1 equals 5m-n over 3.

3
00:00:17.503 --> 00:00:20.816
Step 1. STEP 1.

4
00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:34.430
Key rule: Clearing Fractions (L.C.M.). multiply every term by the L.C.M.. Multiplying by 6 gives 3m minus 6 equals 2(5m-n), removing both denominators.

5
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:49.211
Clear the fractions: multiply both sides by 6 (the LCM of 2 and 3). 6(m over 2 minus 1) equals 6 times 5m-n over 3 which gives 3m minus 6 equals 2(5m-n).

6
00:00:49.631 --> 00:00:53.132
Step 2. STEP 2.

7
00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:59.753
Expand the right-hand side. 3m minus 6 equals 10m minus 2n.

8
00:01:00.173 --> 00:01:03.792
Step 3. STEP 3.

9
00:01:03.952 --> 00:01:14.470
Key rule: Collecting Like Terms. 2n minus 6 equals 7m. Subtracting 3m and adding 6 leaves 7m alone on the right.

10
00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:26.692
Collect the m minus terms on one side. Subtract 3m from both sides and add 6: 2n minus 6 equals 10m minus 3m which gives 2n minus 6 equals 7m.

11
00:01:27.112 --> 00:01:30.590
Step 4. STEP 4.

12
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.964
Divide by 7 to isolate m. m equals 2n minus 6 over 7.

13
00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:40.984
So the answer is: m equals 2n minus 6 over 7.

14
00:01:41.404 --> 00:01:50.177
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 1. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
